# Sensitive paths — require @ctf05 approval to merge changes here.
# Without these rules a contributor could escalate privileges by adding
# malicious entries to ops/manifest.yml or weakening the deploy workflow
# in the same PR they apply a `run-script:` label to.
#
# The rules cover what the production deploy reads or executes, not only the
# workflows: composite actions run inside the deploy job, the environment
# registry decides which secrets are pushed to the Workers, its generator emits
# the secret-push block, the wrangler configs decide what is deployed, and the
# migrations run against the production database.
#
# These rules only enforce review IF branch protection on `main` has
# "Require review from Code Owners" enabled. Verify in repo Settings →
# Branches (or Rulesets) before relying on this protection.

.github/                            @ctf05
ops/                                @ctf05
packages/db/drizzle/                @ctf05
packages/shared/src/env/env.config.ts @ctf05
scripts/generate-env.ts             @ctf05
apps/*/wrangler.toml                @ctf05
